// @check
// @error a `for` range binds one variable, so `i, j` has nothing for `j` to bind — a second name is an index over a sequence or a value over a map
// A RANGE counts ONE value, so a second name has no companion to bind — no index (the loop
// variable IS the count) and no value. Refused at the PARSE tier, anchored at the second name,
// which is the token to delete. A separate file from the checker's `for` refusals because a
// parse error stops the pipeline, so the two tiers cannot be graded together.
for i, j in 0 to 10 {
  print(i)
}
